inked\" can create tension. Soft alliteration in \"white hush\" can calm the mood.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A correction needs to change meaning or accuracy, not just make the text longer.","marking_guide":"Require an actual misconception plus corrected example and purpose-linked explanation.","question":"Name one likely error in using this skill, correct it and explain why the correction helps.","sample_answer":"Common error: Craft talk needs effect, not only naming a technique. Correction: Craft: very short sentences / abrupt rhythm. Effect: shock, suspense, sudden focus.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent task and reflection, with explanations where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-eng-y3-w25-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA alignment; verify content points before acceptance.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise craft.","Read the mission before you start writing or speaking.","Keep the audience and purpose in mind as you work."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reason with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the evidence."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the wording that carries the meaning.","Then explain the choice without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore the example.","Prefer evidence over wording that merely sounds clever."],"submit":["Check that your response and reason are both present.","Proofread names, sequence and punctuation.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact word or action before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and underline one usef